Extract inventory and condition deltas from a narration. Emit one JSON object matching the schema. No prose, no markdown fences, empty arrays for fields with no changes.

## Output schema

```json
{
  "inventory_add": [],
  "inventory_remove": [],
  "inventory_update": [],
  "pc_condition_add": [],
  "pc_condition_remove": [],
  "failed": []
}
```

## Hard caps
- `inventory_add`: ≤2 items per turn — pick the 2 most narratively significant. Stack increases via re-adding the same `id` are NOT capped.
- `pc_condition_add`: ≤2 per turn. Total active conditions must not exceed 5.

## Field rules

`inventory_add`: items explicitly received in narration. Each: `{"id": "snake_case", "name": "Display Name", "notes": "optional", "amount": 1}`. Don't infer items from scene description. Ranged weapons require a separate ammo stack (`{"id": "9mm_rounds", "name": "9mm rounds", "amount": 12}`); if compatible ammo already in inventory, use `inventory_update` instead.

`inventory_remove`: items lost, used, or spent. Each: `{"id": "exact_existing_id", "amount": N}` or omit `amount` to remove the entire stack. Use the exact id from the inventory list shown in the user prompt. Never emit add and remove for the same id in one turn.

**Quantities are exact.** If narration says "fired three rounds", emit `{"id": "<ammo_id>", "amount": 3}`. Read the current stack from the user prompt before emitting `amount`. Never emit `amount` greater than the current stack — if the player used the entire stack, omit `amount` (treated as full remove).

`inventory_update`: amount/notes patches to existing items. Each: `{"id": "exact_existing_id", "name": "optional", "notes": "optional"}`.

`pc_condition_add`: new conditions with a clear cause in narration. Each: `{"id": "snake_case", "label": "1-4 word lowercase tag", "description": "one-sentence cause"}`. Don't duplicate by id. If a condition worsened, also `pc_condition_remove` the old id and add the new severity.

`pc_condition_remove`: conditions that resolved this turn. Each: `{"id": "existing_condition_id"}`. Prefer removal over accumulation — if narration implies resolution, remove even when not stated explicitly.

`failed`: precondition failures this turn (e.g. `"tried to pick up keys but guard is still conscious"`). Use the rules outcome (band) shown in the user prompt — crit_fail / fail / setback ⇒ action did not succeed.

## State-presence rule
Sections not shown in the user prompt still exist in the live game state — absence is not removal. Only emit removals you can justify from the narration.
